0.0057099997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Sprouts Farmers Market, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the retailing of fresh, natural, and organic food products in the United States. The company operates healthy grocery stores; and lifestyle-friendly ingredients, such as organic, plant-based, keto, paleo, non-GMO, and gluten-free. The company also offers perishable product categories, including produce, meat and meat alternatives, seafood, deli, bakery, floral, and dairy alternatives; and non-perishable product categories, such as grocery, vitamins and supplements, bulk items, frozen foods, beer and wine, and natural health and body care. It sells its products under the Sprouts brand. The company was founded in 1943 and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jack L. Sinclair | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 36K people. Revenue per employee of $245K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $864 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 20\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Sprouts Farmers Market, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $4.8B market cap on $8.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 30% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 22-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 34%.","The business throws off $468M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 24% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in SFM Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_SFM_Response_111326010202_1794592922.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794592922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"RD MANAGEMENT CELEBRATES GRAND OPENING OF LA FITNESS ELEVATE AT RITHM AT UPTOWN","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/rd-management-celebrates-grand-opening-193100600.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794598260.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.982,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Friday Checkout: Winn-Dixie bets on its Florida roots","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/small-business/articles/friday-checkout-winn-dixie-bets-140635597.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578795.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Not Pumpkin, Not Pecan: The Seasonal Grocery Store Pie Shoppers Say Is 'The Best' They've 'Ever Tasted'","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/not-pumpkin-not-pecan-seasonal-191126000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794518063.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.925,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Beachbody: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles